The demonstration presents LegalEase as a working product in about five to seven minutes. It starts with a one-sentence statement of the problem, and then the presenter logs in and chooses a document such as a rental agreement. The presenter answers the guided questions and shows the generated draft together with the plain-language explanation of its clauses. One clause is then edited and saved, the document is downloaded as a PDF, and the dashboard is shown with the saved versions. The accompanying presentation covers the problem, the proposed solution, the architecture and technology stack, the live demo, the testing results, the challenges faced, the limitations, and the future scope. Common questions from evaluators can be answered briefly. On legal validity, LegalEase produces drafts and recommends review by a licensed lawyer for complex matters. On AI errors, the system uses vetted templates, output validation, and disclaimers. On data protection, it relies on encryption, minimal storage, and secure authentication. Future improvements include support for more languages and jurisdictions, electronic signatures, a marketplace for lawyer review, voice input, and a mobile application.
